{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"312eae5b7bc8e621","name":"card_unit_175th_motorized","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Legions/units/card_unit_175th_motorized","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"175th MOTORIZED","text":"Destruction: All your Soviet tanks in hand and deck cost 1 less to deploy.","flavorText":"The 175th Motorized Rifle Regiment was a unit of the 1st Moscow Motor Rifle Division of the Soviet Red Army. In 1940 the division took part in the Soviet occupation of the Baltic states, but in 1941, during Operation Barbarossa, it was called back to Moscow where it joined the 7th Mechanised Corps in defending against the German advance. That same year the division participated in heavy fighting near Smolensk, where it was encircled and annihilated, but reformed again later in the year and renamed to the 1st Guards Moscow Motor Rifle Division. Throughout the war the division participated in numerous battles and operations, including the Moscow counteroffensive in 1942, the Battle of Rzhev, and Operation Kutuzov which was the first of two counteroffensives during the Kursk Strategic Offensive Operation in 1943. Finally, in April 1945, the division took part in storming and liberating the town of Baltiysk from German occupation.","faction":"Soviet","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_175th_motorized","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_175th_motorized_title","SourceString":"175th MOTORIZED","LocalizedString":"175th MOTORIZED"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_175th_motorized_text","SourceString":"Destruction: All your Soviet tanks in hand and deck cost 1 less to deploy.","LocalizedString":"Destruction: All your Soviet tanks in hand and deck cost 1 less to deploy."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_175th_motorized_history","SourceString":"The 175th Motorized Rifle Regiment was a unit of the 1st Moscow Motor Rifle Division of the Soviet Red Army. In 1940 the division took part in the Soviet occupation of the Baltic states, but in 1941, during Operation Barbarossa, it was called back to Moscow where it joined the 7th Mechanised Corps in defending against the German advance. That same year the division participated in heavy fighting near Smolensk, where it was encircled and annihilated, but reformed again later in the year and renamed to the 1st Guards Moscow Motor Rifle Division. Throughout the war the division participated in numerous battles and operations, including the Moscow counteroffensive in 1942, the Battle of Rzhev, and Operation Kutuzov which was the first of two counteroffensives during the Kursk Strategic Offensive Operation in 1943. Finally, in April 1945, the division took part in storming and liberating the town of Baltiysk from German occupation.","LocalizedString":"The 175th Motorized Rifle Regiment was a unit of the 1st Moscow Motor Rifle Division of the Soviet Red Army. In 1940 the division took part in the Soviet occupation of the Baltic states, but in 1941, during Operation Barbarossa, it was called back to Moscow where it joined the 7th Mechanised Corps in defending against the German advance. That same year the division participated in heavy fighting near Smolensk, where it was encircled and annihilated, but reformed again later in the year and renamed to the 1st Guards Moscow Motor Rifle Division. Throughout the war the division participated in numerous battles and operations, including the Moscow counteroffensive in 1942, the Battle of Rzhev, and Operation Kutuzov which was the first of two counteroffensives during the Kursk Strategic Offensive Operation in 1943. Finally, in April 1945, the division took part in storming and liberating the town of Baltiysk from German occupation."},"operationCost":1,"rari